# Workflows

## Commands

```sh
cargo build                          # whole workspace
cargo test --workspace               # unit tests (state runtime, tailwind compiler)

# Native desktop windows (examples are registered as bins):
cargo run --bin 01_hello_world
cargo run --bin 02_counter_app
cargo run --bin 03_todo_app
cargo run --bin 04_elements
```

## Web (Trunk + wasm32)

Examples are registered as `[[bin]]` targets precisely so Trunk can build them —
no extra glue is needed; `launch()` handles the web event loop and canvas setup.
Each example has its own HTML shell in `web/` that selects the bin via `data-bin`.

```sh
rustup target add wasm32-unknown-unknown
cargo install trunk --locked
trunk serve web/02_counter_app.html   # default target, serves on :8080
trunk serve web/01_hello_world.html
trunk serve web/03_todo_app.html
trunk build --release web/03_todo_app.html   # output in dist/
```

The default target in `Trunk.toml` is `web/02_counter_app.html`. The `web/*.html`
shells load the Rust bin with `<link data-trunk data-type="rust" data-bin="..."/>`;
add a new shell file per new example bin.

## Gotchas

- First native build of `wgpu` is slow; `wgpu-core`/`wgpu-types` have opt-level 1 in dev.
- On macOS the app must run from the main thread (winit requirement) — the runtime does
  this; don't spawn winit windows on background threads.
- If a window opens blank: the render effect only repaints on `RedrawRequested`; check
  that state writes happened (no writes = paint-once) and that `Renderer` was created
  (on wasm it's async — `ready` is set after `spawn_local` completes).
- winit 0.30 delivers keyboard modifiers via a separate `ModifiersChanged` event; the
  runtime caches them in `Shared.modifiers` — don't read them off `KeyEvent`.

## Extending the framework

- **New Tailwind class** → `crates/html_rs_core/src/style.rs` (`apply`) + test.
- **New color** → `crates/html_rs_core/src/colors.rs` (palette macro; shades ordered
  50→950).
- **New element behavior** (e.g. checkbox, scroll) → hit targets/paint logic in
  `crates/html_rs_render/src/painter.rs`; dispatch in `src/runtime.rs`.
- **New event attribute** in `ui!` → add to `EVENTS` table in
  `crates/html_rs_macro/src/lib.rs` + a constructor fn in `crates/html_rs_core/src/element.rs`
  (`click`, `input`, `enter`, `key` are the existing ones).
- **New GPU feature** (shadows, gradients, images) → new pipeline in
  `crates/html_rs_render/src/lib.rs`; quads are premultiplied-alpha, sRGB→linear converted.
